{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-0f0a939d-d9c1-46e1-8bc0-6d3673920c75","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-ba854b1f8f756738","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8002-4x80a8hn/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8002-E002.md","content":"# Kueue Management Indicators for Projects and Workbenches\n\n## Description\n\nAdd visibility indicators to the odh-dashboard so users can tell whether\ntheir project uses queue-based scheduling: a positive Kueue indicator on the\nproject details page for Kueue-managed namespaces, and an anomaly indicator\non individual workbenches that are NOT managed by Kueue inside a Kueue-managed\nnamespace. Development proceeds with a placeholder visual treatment; the\nfinal treatment is swapped in when the UX design deliverable\n(RHOAIUX-7470) lands and must not block this epic.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Project details page: display a positive indicator (info banner, badge, or\n  label — final form per UX decision, placeholder during development) when\n  the namespace has the `kueue.openshift.io/managed=true` label. The\n  requirement is non-negotiable: users must know their project uses\n  queue-based scheduling because it affects how their workloads start.\n- Workbenches overview: for a namespace that IS Kueue-managed, show a visual\n  anomaly indicator only on workbenches that are NOT managed by Kueue\n  (missing the `kueue.x-k8s.io/queue-name` label — e.g. created via GitOps or\n  CLI bypassing the dashboard). Do NOT show \"managed by Kueue\" on every\n  workload in a Kueue-managed namespace; only the anomaly is flagged.\n- Warning about missing queue labels must never block workload creation.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a Kueue-managed namespace, when the user views the project details\n  page, then a positive indicator is visible stating this project uses\n  queue-based scheduling, measured by the indicator element being present in\n  the DOM when the namespace label `kueue.openshift.io/managed=true` exists\n  and absent when it does not.\n- Given a Kueue-managed namespace containing a workbench that does NOT have\n  the `kueue.x-k8s.io/queue-name` label (created via GitOps or CLI without\n  queue assignment), when the user views the workbenches overview, then that\n  specific workbench displays a visual indicator that it is not managed by\n  Kueue, measured by the anomaly indicator being present only on non-Kueue\n  workloads and absent on Kueue-managed workloads.\n- A placeholder visual treatment is in place from the start; the final UX\n  treatment is integrated when delivered, without reworking the underlying\n  condition logic.\n- No workload creation is blocked due to a missing queue label; at most a\n  warning is shown.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- [P0] Add positive Kueue indicator on project details page when namespace\n  has `kueue.openshift.io/managed=true` label.\n- [P0] Add anomaly indicator on workloads in a Kueue-managed namespace that\n  are NOT managed by Kueue (missing `kueue.x-k8s.io/queue-name` label).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":59708,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9742b1d84389a157","agent_id":"a9a69b6d8b27c69c8","session_id":"56884f6e-5c85-4514-8d3c-714b4e528234","uuid":"8e0da889-9604-4a1b-b91d-5b42dbc3ab37","timestamp":"2026-10-22T08:53:24.235Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8002"}
