{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-0f0a939d-d9c1-46e1-8bc0-6d3673920c75","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a574f5c92b2ecd8","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8002-4x80a8hn/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8002-E003.md","content":"# Kueue Visibility API Queue Position Integration\n\n## Description\n\nIntegrate Kueue's Visibility API (`visibility.kueue.x-k8s.io`) into the\nodh-dashboard to display queue position for pending workloads in the\nworkbenches overview. Queue position is not a field on the Workload object —\nit lives on the `PendingWorkload` type served by the Visibility API's\n`PendingWorkloadsSummary` subresources on queues. All calls go through the\n`/api/k8s` passthrough proxy with the logged-in user's token and are subject\nto the user's RBAC.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Add a frontend API client for the Kueue Visibility API\n  (`visibility.kueue.x-k8s.io/v1beta2`), reading the `pendingworkloads`\n  subresource on LocalQueues:\n  `GET /apis/visibility.kueue.x-k8s.io/v1beta2/namespaces/{ns}/localqueues/{name}/pendingworkloads`.\n- Display `positionInLocalQueue` (and `positionInClusterQueue` where\n  available) for pending workloads in the workbenches overview.\n- Graceful degradation on 403: a 403 on the Visibility API must fail\n  silently — position info is supplementary, not critical. Use the existing\n  `getGenericErrorCode` pattern from `DistributedWorkloadsContext.tsx`.\n- ClusterQueue-level position (`/clusterqueues/{name}/pendingworkloads`) is\n  cluster-scoped and admin-only; include only if it fits the same mechanism\n  without extra RBAC assumptions.\n- Validate whether RHOAI clusters bind data scientists to Kubernetes roles\n  (`batch-user`, `view`, `admin`, `edit`) that aggregate Kueue's\n  `pending-workloads-lq-viewer-role` ClusterRole, and document the finding\n  for the position-UI polish investment decision.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a workbench is in QueuingPending state and the user's token has\n  `batch-user` RBAC to the Visibility API, when the workbenches overview page\n  renders, then the queue position is displayed (position in local queue),\n  measured by the position number being present and matching the value from\n  the `pendingworkloads` subresource.\n- Given a workbench is in QueuingPending state and the user's token does NOT\n  have RBAC to the Visibility API, when the workbenches overview page\n  renders, then the queue position is silently omitted with no error\n  displayed, measured by the absence of both position data and error\n  indicators.\n- The RBAC availability validation is documented: if data scientists do not\n  hold aggregating role bindings by default, position display is effectively\n  admin-only and this is recorded as a known limitation (403 handling covers\n  regular users).\n- Existing workbench behavior is unchanged when Kueue is not enabled.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- [P1] Integrate Kueue Visibility API for queue position display\n  (`positionInLocalQueue`, `positionInClusterQueue`) via\n  `PendingWorkloadsSummary` subresource on LocalQueue — gracefully degrade\n  on 403.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":59708,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9742b1d84389a157","agent_id":"a9a69b6d8b27c69c8","session_id":"56884f6e-5c85-4514-8d3c-714b4e528234","uuid":"97fdfad6-4022-4162-b1bc-d005db67cc98","timestamp":"2026-10-22T08:53:33.135Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8002"}
