{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-0f0a939d-d9c1-46e1-8bc0-6d3673920c75","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-90a62958f7eb9987","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8002-4x80a8hn/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8002-E004.md","content":"# HardwareProfile Scheduling UX: GitOps Popover Fallback, LocalQueue Validation, and Dropdown Guidance\n\n## Description\n\nHarden the HardwareProfile (HP) scheduling surfaces in the odh-dashboard for\nKueue-managed namespaces: fix the HP details popover for GitOps-managed\nnotebooks that carry the queue label directly, add LocalQueue name validation\nto the HP admin form, and explain why the HP dropdown only shows queue-enabled\nprofiles in Kueue-managed namespaces.\n\n## Scope\n\n- HP details popover fallback for GitOps-managed notebooks: when a notebook\n  has `kueue.x-k8s.io/queue-name` applied directly (no matching\n  HardwareProfile — a supported RHBoK pattern), the popover reads the queue\n  label from the notebook's own labels, resolves the cluster queue name from\n  the project's LocalQueue list, and indicates the source: \"Queue: my-queue\n  (applied directly)\" vs. \"Queue: my-queue (via hardware profile)\".\n- HardwareProfile admin form: validate the LocalQueue name field against\n  `k8sNameRegex` (`/^[a-z0-9]([-a-z0-9]*[a-z0-9])?$/`). Existence of the\n  LocalQueue cannot be validated at HP creation time (HPs are cluster-scoped,\n  LocalQueues are namespace-scoped, target namespace unknown).\n- Workbench creation time: if the specified LocalQueue does not exist in the\n  target namespace, display a warning — NOT an error. The admin may have\n  intended the LQ to be created later or delivered via GitOps; Kueue itself\n  reports the error via the Workload's conditions if the queue truly doesn't\n  exist (eventually consistent systems).\n- HP dropdown in the workbench creation form: keep strict filtering (only\n  queue-based HPs in Kueue-managed namespaces) but add an explicit info\n  indicator (info icon or tooltip) explaining \"Only queue-enabled hardware\n  profiles are shown because this project uses queue-based scheduling.\"\n  Placeholder copy is acceptable until the UX content review delivers final\n  wording.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a GitOps-managed workbench with `kueue.x-k8s.io/queue-name` label\n  applied directly (no matching HardwareProfile), when the user opens the\n  HardwareProfile details popover, then the popover displays the queue name\n  with indication it was applied directly (not via hardware profile),\n  measured by the popover text including the queue name and a source\n  indicator.\n- Given an admin is creating a HardwareProfile and enters an invalid\n  LocalQueue name (e.g. contains uppercase or spaces), when the form\n  validates, then a validation error is shown for the LocalQueue name field,\n  measured by the form displaying an inline error referencing the Kubernetes\n  name format.\n- Given a workbench is being created with a HardwareProfile referencing a\n  LocalQueue that does not exist in the target namespace, when the creation\n  form is submitted, then a warning (not error) is displayed indicating the\n  local queue was not found, measured by the warning being dismissible and\n  not blocking workbench creation.\n- Given a workbench is in a Kueue-managed namespace and the user opens the\n  workbench creation form, when the HardwareProfile dropdown renders with\n  only queue-enabled profiles, then an info indicator explains why only\n  queue-enabled profiles are shown, measured by the presence of a tooltip or\n  info icon adjacent to the dropdown.\n- Strict filtering behavior of the HP dropdown is unchanged.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- [P1] Fix HardwareProfile details popover for GitOps-managed notebooks:\n  read queue label directly when no HP match exists, indicate source.\n- [P1] Add `k8sNameRegex` validation to LocalQueue name field in\n  HardwareProfile admin form.\n- [P1] Add explicit info indicator on HP dropdown explaining why only\n  queue-enabled profiles are shown in Kueue-managed namespaces.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":59708,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9742b1d84389a157","agent_id":"a9a69b6d8b27c69c8","session_id":"56884f6e-5c85-4514-8d3c-714b4e528234","uuid":"bf4c85d9-4a18-4287-bec2-3eb848ca9698","timestamp":"2026-10-22T08:53:43.843Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8002"}
