ins for\n  unknown conditions only).\n- Copy is approved through the UXD content review (RHOAIUX-7470).\n- Override wording is delivered in a form that drops into the dashboard's\n  override lookup table without changes to the fallback mechanism.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- [P0] Display workload scheduling status derived from Workload CR\n  conditions with human-friendly message overrides and raw message fallback\n  (final wording; the override mechanism and placeholder copy are delivered\n  by the status model implementation).\n- [P2] Improve status message granularity: distinguish WaitForRecovery from\n  WaitForStart, surface AdmissionCheck pending/retry states (wording for the\n  newly distinguished states).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":62389,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9742b1d84389a157","agent_id":"a9a69b6d8b27c69c8","session_id":"56884f6e-5c85-4514-8d3c-714b4e528234","uuid":"a463e475-29ff-4bce-b229-b29ecc6b77b8","timestamp":"2026-10-22T08:53:55.264Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8002"}
