{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9c68f8722a13f0a5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8002-E002\n3\ttitle: Kueue management indicators for projects and workbenches\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8002\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Dashboard\n6\tteam: Dashboard UI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 1\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 0\n15\t  external_dependency: 1\n16\t  human_process_gates: 0\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Kueue Management Indicators for Projects and Workbenches\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tAdd visibility indicators to the odh-dashboard so users can tell whether\n34\ttheir project uses queue-based scheduling: a positive Kueue indicator on the\n35\tproject details page for Kueue-managed namespaces, and an anomaly indicator\n36\ton individual workbenches that are NOT managed by Kueue inside a Kueue-managed\n37\tnamespace. Development proceeds with a placeholder visual treatment; the\n38\tfinal treatment is swapped in when the UX design deliverable\n39\t(RHOAIUX-7470) lands and must not block this epic.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Project details page: display a positive indicator (info banner, badge, or\n44\t  label — final form per UX decision, placeholder during development) when\n45\t  the namespace has the `kueue.openshift.io/managed=true` label. The\n46\t  requirement is non-negotiable: users must know their project uses\n47\t  queue-based scheduling because it affects how their workloads start.\n48\t- Workbenches overview: for a namespace that IS Kueue-managed, show a visual\n49\t  anomaly indicator only on workbenches that are NOT managed by Kueue\n50\t  (missing the `kueue.x-k8s.io/queue-name` label — e.g. created via GitOps or\n51\t  CLI bypassing the dashboard). Do NOT show \"managed by Kueue\" on every\n52\t  workload in a Kueue-managed namespace; only the anomaly is flagged.\n53\t- Warning about missing queue labels must never block workload creation.\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- Given a Kueue-managed namespace, when the user views the project details\n58\t  page, then a positive indicator is visible stating this project uses\n59\t  queue-based scheduling, measured by the indicator element being present in\n60\t  the DOM when the namespace label `kueue.openshift.io/managed=true` exists\n61\t  and absent when it does not.\n62\t- Given a Kueue-managed namespace containing a workbench that does NOT have\n63\t  the `kueue.x-k8s.io/queue-name` label (created via GitOps or CLI without\n64\t  queue assignment), when the user views the workbenches overview, then that\n65\t  specific workbench displays a visual indicator that it is not managed by\n66\t  Kueue, measured by the anomaly indicator being present only on non-Kueue\n67\t  workloads and absent on Kueue-managed workloads.\n68\t- A placeholder visual treatment is in place from the start; the final UX\n69\t  treatment is integrated when delivered, without reworking the underlying\n70\t  condition logic.\n71\t- No workload creation is blocked due to a missing queue label; at most a\n72\t  warning is shown.\n73\t\n74\t## HLR Traceability\n75\t\n76\t- [P0] Add positive Kueue indicator on project details page when namespace\n77\t  has `kueue.openshift.io/managed=true` label.\n78\t- [P0] Add anomaly indicator on workloads in a Kueue-managed namespace that\n79\t  are NOT managed by Kueue (missing `kueue.x-k8s.io/queue-name` label).\n80\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bb296e02b4f4740c","agent_id":"ab636a87a47f19bee","session_id":"56884f6e-5c85-4514-8d3c-714b4e528234","uuid":"d8570002-9e43-4b2a-9efc-7151a9198604","timestamp":"2026-10-22T08:56:47.426Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9c68f8722a13f0a5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8002 decomposition"}
