{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a49783f662744411","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8002-E005\n3\ttitle: Human-friendly Kueue status message content\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8002\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Dashboard\n6\tteam: Content\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8002-E001\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 1\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n15\t  existing_foundation: 0\n16\t  open_questions: 0\n17\t  external_dependency: 1\n18\t  human_process_gates: -1\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 3\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Human-Friendly Kueue Status Message Content\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tAuthor the final human-readable status message wording for Kueue Workload\n35\tcondition/reason combinations displayed in the workbenches overview. The\n36\tengineering implementation ships with reasonable default overrides and a\n37\traw-message fallback; this deliverable replaces the placeholder copy with\n38\treviewed, user-facing wording for data scientists and platform operators, and\n39\tis reviewed through the UXD content review (RHOAIUX-7470).\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Author human-friendly override copy for all known Workload condition/reason\n44\t  combinations, including at minimum: the eviction reasons (Preempted,\n45\t  PodsReadyTimeout, AdmissionCheck, ClusterQueueStopped, LocalQueueStopped,\n46\t  Deactivated, NodeFailures, MaximumExecutionTimeExceeded), the Requeued\n47\t  state (retry count, next retry time), AdmissionCheck pending/retry states,\n48\t  and the distinction between WaitForRecovery and WaitForStart.\n49\t- Word copy for data scientists who are not Kubernetes-savvy: raw Kueue\n50\t  condition messages are unintelligible to them; the overrides must explain\n51\t  what is happening and what (if anything) the user can do.\n52\t- Deliver the copy in the form consumable by the dashboard's message override\n53\t  lookup table (final wording replaces the engineering placeholders).\n54\t- Incorporate content review feedback from UXD (RHOAIUX-7470).\n55\t\n56\t## Acceptance Criteria\n57\t\n58\t- Every known condition/reason combination in the dashboard's status model\n59\t  has a reviewed human-friendly override; no known combination falls through\n60\t  to the raw message by omission (the raw-message fallback remains for\n61\t  unknown conditions only).\n62\t- Copy is approved through the UXD content review (RHOAIUX-7470).\n63\t- Override wording is delivered in a form that drops into the dashboard's\n64\t  override lookup table without changes to the fallback mechanism.\n65\t\n66\t## HLR Traceability\n67\t\n68\t- [P0] Display workload scheduling status derived from Workload CR\n69\t  conditions with human-friendly message overrides and raw message fallback\n70\t  (final wording; the override mechanism and placeholder copy are delivered\n71\t  by the status model implementation).\n72\t- [P2] Improve status message granularity: distinguish WaitForRecovery from\n73\t  WaitForStart, surface AdmissionCheck pending/retry states (wording for the\n74\t  newly distinguished states).\n75\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bb296e02b4f4740c","agent_id":"ab636a87a47f19bee","session_id":"56884f6e-5c85-4514-8d3c-714b4e528234","uuid":"58880fb6-5b02-42f8-928f-6cab63c4bb0b","timestamp":"2026-10-22T08:56:55.662Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a49783f662744411","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8002 decomposition"}
