 why only queue-enabled profiles are shown in Kueue-managed\n50\t  namespaces, including copy.\n51\t- Specify treatments using the existing PatternFly-based design system so\n52\t  they are directly implementable in the dashboard.\n53\t- Participate in the content review of the human-friendly status message\n54\t  overrides (final copy approval happens in the content deliverable's review\n55\t  gate).\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- Visual treatment for the positive Kueue indicator is decided and specified\n60\t  (banner/badge/label), with copy, ready for implementation.\n61\t- Visual treatment for the workload anomaly indicator is specified, with copy\n62\t  and placement, ready for implementation.\n63\t- Visual treatment for the HardwareProfile dropdown info indicator is\n64\t  specified, with copy, ready for implementation.\n65\t- Designs are delivered through RHOAIUX-7470 and consumable by the dashboard\n66\t  implementation without further design exploration.\n67\t\n68\t## HLR Traceability\n69\t\n70\t- [P0] Add positive Kueue indicator on project details page (final visual\n71\t  treatment; the indicator logic and placeholder render are delivered by the\n72\t  dashboard implementation).\n73\t- [P0] Add anomaly indicator on workloads in a Kueue-managed namespace that\n74\t  are NOT managed by Kueue (final visual treatment).\n75\t- [P1] Add explicit info indicator on HP dropdown explaining why only\n76\t  queue-enabled profiles are shown (final visual treatment and copy).\n77\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bb296e02b4f4740c","agent_id":"ab636a87a47f19bee","session_id":"56884f6e-5c85-4514-8d3c-714b4e528234","uuid":"4939347c-4bf2-4e6b-bbde-67d2e8c7488d","timestamp":"2026-10-22T08:56:56.608Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8e4f20ac1fc3951d","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8002 decomposition"}
