e implementation\nwith content authoring. E001 is the largest epic but is a single coherent\nstatus-model rework inside an S-sized strategy — not clearly multi-sprint.\n\n### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n\nNo Investigation epics, and the scan correctly applies the decision rule to\nboth strategy open questions: the Visibility API RBAC aggregation question\ndoes not change epic structure (both outcomes are handled by the same E003\nepic via 403 degradation, recorded as a validation AC), and the indicator\nform question is neutralized by the placeholder-treatment directive (E006\ntracks the design deliverable). All seven epics are Implementation and\nproduce concrete artifacts. No `gated_by` fields are set and none are needed\n(no Investigation dependencies exist), so no gating metadata issues.\n\n### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n\nAll seven epics are Implementation type and carry the 9-signal `ai_signals`\nfield with `investigation_signals: null` — the correct rubric per type.\nFrontmatter values match the ai-signals rationale tables exactly for all\nseven epics. Signal differentiation is justified by epic content: E005\n`human_process_gates: -1` (UXD content review gate on final wording), E006\n`repo_access: 0` (design artifacts in design tooling, not a clonable repo)\nand `ai_implementability: Medium`, E003 `pattern_precedent: 0` (new\naggregated-API integration). Borderline calls — E002 `open_questions: 0`\n(pending UX form, neutralized by placeholder directive) and E003\n`external_dependency: 0` (Beta API availability assumed confirmed) — are\neach supported by an explicit rationale citing the neutralizing strategy\nconstraint. Computed aggregates were not checked per instructions.\n\n### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n\nEvery epic has testable, measurable ACs. All 11 strategy acceptance criteria\nare carried into epic ACs essentially verbatim (E001: eviction distinction,\nRequeued retry info, raw-message fallback; E002: positive and anomaly\nindicators; E003: position displayed / silently omitted on 403; E004:\npopover fallback, regex validation, missing-LQ warning, dropdown info\nindicator). Rule-mandated ACs are present where applicable: E007\n(docs-authoring) has technical-review ACs; there is no konflux chain (N/A);\nthe purely-additive/conditional NFR is carried as backwards-compatibility\nACs on E001, E002, and E003. No epic body references sibling epics by draft\nID — the only ticket references are the real RHOAIUX-7470 key.\n\n### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n\nFull scope coverage: all 11 HLRs mapped, all four NFRs carried as ACs\n(unknown-condition raw fallback, 403 silent degradation, additive/conditional\nbackwards compat), all three risks carried forward (RBAC → E003 validation\nAC; message resonance → E005; GitOps hybrid users → E002 anomaly indicator),\nand both open questions tracked (E003 AC; E006 design deliverable with E002\nplaceholder). Documentation Support is required → E007 `docs-authoring` epic\nis present (Rule 11). The AI-generated over-promises (quota/resource\ncolumns, estimated wait times, historical queue data) are correctly dropped\nper Staff input, with the overrides documented in the summary. Conditional\nbranches are not used and are not needed (no bounded-outcome uncertainty).\n\nMinor: the strategy's success criteria \"Performance: UI remains responsive\nwith Kueue integration\" and \"Scalability: Handles large numbers of queued\nworkloads\" are not carried as explicit ACs on E003, the performance-relevant\nepic that adds per-queue API calls.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32424,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bb296e02b4f4740c","agent_id":"ab636a87a47f19bee","session_id":"56884f6e-5c85-4514-8d3c-714b4e528234","uuid":"da927793-4056-4772-94fe-caa5990b4e24","timestamp":"2026-10-22T09:00:48.409Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8002 dec