inside an S-sized strategy — not clearly multi-sprint.\n107\t\n108\t### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n109\t\n110\tNo Investigation epics, and the scan correctly applies the decision rule to\n111\tboth strategy open questions: the Visibility API RBAC aggregation question\n112\tdoes not change epic structure (both outcomes are handled by the same E003\n113\tepic via 403 degradation, recorded as a validation AC), and the indicator\n114\tform question is neutralized by the placeholder-treatment directive (E006\n115\ttracks the design deliverable). All seven epics are Implementation and\n116\tproduce concrete artifacts. No `gated_by` fields are set and none are needed\n117\t(no Investigation dependencies exist), so no gating metadata issues.\n118\t\n119\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n120\t\n121\tAll seven epics are Implementation type and carry the 9-signal `ai_signals`\n122\tfield with `investigation_signals: null` — the correct rubric per type.\n123\tFrontmatter values match the ai-signals rationale tables exactly for all\n124\tseven epics. Signal differentiation is justified by epic content: E005\n125\t`human_process_gates: -1` (UXD content review gate on final wording), E006\n126\t`repo_access: 0` (design artifacts in design tooling, not a clonable repo)\n127\tand `ai_implementability: Medium`, E003 `pattern_precedent: 0` (new\n128\taggregated-API integration). Borderline calls — E002 `open_questions: 0`\n129\t(pending UX form, neutralized by placeholder directive) and E003\n130\t`external_dependency: 0` (Beta API availability assumed confirmed) — are\n131\teach supported by an explicit rationale citing the neutralizing strategy\n132\tconstraint. Computed aggregates were not checked per instructions.\n133\t\n134\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n135\t\n136\tEvery epic has testable, measurable ACs. All 11 strategy acceptance criteria\n137\tare carried into epic ACs essentially verbatim (E001: eviction distinction,\n138\tRequeued retry info, raw-messa