{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9fd3838eed3bca8c","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8002\n3\tepic_count: 7\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\t---\n9\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-8002\n10\t\n11\tIntegrate Kueue workload scheduling information in the Workbenches overview (odh-dashboard).\n12\t\n13\t## Triage Note\n14\t\n15\tThe strategy is S-sized and affects a single component (odh-dashboard), but the\n16\tbelow-threshold path was **not** taken: the scope spans multiple distinct work\n17\tstreams — frontend code implementation (Dashboard UI), substantive content\n18\tauthoring (status message microcopy, Content team), UX design deliverables\n19\t(UXD), and documentation (Docs) — that warrant separate review cycles and are\n20\towned by different teams. Full decomposition follows.\n21\t\n22\t## Staff Engineer Input Overrides (traceability)\n23\t\n24\tThe Staff Engineer / SME Input section takes precedence over the AI-generated\n25\tstrategy sections. Overrides applied:\n26\t\n27\t1. **rhods-operator removed from Affected Components.** The HardwareProfile\n28\t   mutating webhook that injects the `kueue.x-k8s.io/queue-name` label is out\n29\t   of scope; all work is odh-dashboard frontend.\n30\t2. **Resource/quota visibility dropped.** The AI-generated \"Proposed Solution\"\n31\t   promises a \"Resources: Requested vs. available\" column; Staff input rules\n32\t   this out — LocalQueues carry no quota information, quota lives at the\n33\t   ClusterQueue level, and data scientists may lack RBAC to read it.\n34\t3. **Estimated wait time dropped.** The AI-generated sections mention estimated\n35\t   wait times and historical queue patterns; out of scope — Kueue does not\n36\t   provide wait-time prediction, only factual queue position and elapsed time.\n37\t4. **Status model is state-driven.** The AI-generated status indicator set\n38\t   (Admitted/Pending/Running/Suspended) is superseded by the Staff-directed\n39\t   model: status derived from Workload CR conditions and pod/container\n40\t   statuses, with human-friendly overrides and raw-message fallback.\n41\t5. **Dependencies reduced.** The only dependency retained is UXD finalized\n42\t   designs and content (RHOAIUX-7470), which explicitly must NOT block\n43\t   development. Other listed dependencies were moved to Assumptions.\n44\t\n45\t## Component Mapping\n46\t\n47\t- `odh-dashboard` → canonical Jira component **AI Core Dashboard** (from\n48\t  `.context/rhai-components.txt`; no exact \"odh-dashboard\" entry exists).\n49\t- Documentation epic → component **Documentation**.\n50\t- odh-dashboard exists in `.context/architecture-context/`\n51\t  (`architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/odh-dashboard.md`) — component is in the\n52\t  platform; no onboarding chain (repo/license/konflux) is generated.\n53\t\n54\t## Epic List\n55\t\n56\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n57\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n58\t| RHAISTRAT-8002-E001 | Workload scheduling status model and display in workbenches overview | Implementation | Dashboard UI | P0 |\n59\t| RHAISTRAT-8002-E002 | Kueue management indicators for projects and workbenches | Implementation | Dashboard UI | P0 |\n60\t| RHAISTRAT-8002-E003 | Kueue Visibility API queue position integration | Implementation | Dashboard UI | P1 |\n61\t| RHAISTRAT-8002-E004 | HardwareProfile scheduling UX: GitOps popover fallback, LocalQueue validation, and dropdown guidance | Implementation | Dashboard UI | P1 |\n62\t| RHAISTRAT-8002-E005 | Human-friendly Kueue status message content | Implementation | Content | P0 |\n63\t| RHAISTRAT-8002-E006 | UX design for Kueue visibility indicators | Implementation | UXD | P0 |\n64\t| RHAISTRAT-8002-E007 | Documentation for Kueue workload scheduling visibility | Implementation (docs-authoring) | Docs | P1 |\n65\t\n66\t## Dependency DAG\n67\t\n68\t```mermaid\n69\tgraph TD\n70\t    E001[\"E001 Status model & display\"]\n71\t    E002[\"E002 Kueue indicators\"]\n72\t    E003[\"E003 Visibility API position\"]\n73\t    E004[\"E004 HardwareProfile UX\"]\n74\t    E005[\"E005 Status message content\"]\n75\t    E006[\"E006 UX design\"]\n76\t    E007[\"E007 Documentation\"]\n77\t    E001 --> E005\n78\t    E001 --> E007\n79\t    E002 --> E007\n80\t    E003 --> E007\n81\t    E004 --> E007\n82\t    E005 --> E007\n83\t    E006 --> E007\n84\t```\n85\t\n86\t## DAG Justification\n87\t\n88\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n89\t|------|------|-----------|\n90\t| E001 → E005 | Rule 13 (artifact consumer) | The message-override copy is authored against the enumerated Workload condition/reason set and the override mechanism produced by the status-model implementation; content work builds on that artifact. |\n91\t| E001 → E007 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring last) | Documentation is blocked by all Implementation epics; docs describe what was built. |\n92\t| E002 → E007 | Rule 11 | Same. |\n93\t| E003 → E007 | Rule 11 | Same. |\n94\t| E004 → E007 | Rule 11 | Same. |\n95\t| E005 → E007 | Rule 11 | Same. |\n96\t| E006 → E007 | Rule 11 | Same. |\n97\t| E001 ∥ E002 ∥ E003 ∥ E004 (no edges) | Rule 15 | Same repo, different areas: status derivation from Workload CRs, namespace/workload label indicators, a new aggregated API integration, and HardwareProfile forms. No shared data structures or API endpoints between them; merge-conflict risk is coordination, not dependency. |\n98\t| E006 ∥ all implementation epics (no edges) | Strategy constraint | Development must NOT be blocked on UX answers. The final visual treatment is swapped in at execution time via an acceptance criterion on the indicator epic (placeholder copy/treatment during development), not via a DAG dependency. |\n99\t| E002 ∥ E005 (no edge) | Rule 14 | Different teams, independent surfaces (UI indicator components vs. status message strings); no shared artifact. |\n100\t\n101\t## Investigation Scan Result\n102\t\n103\tNo Investigation epics. The strategy's two open questions were evaluated with\n104\tthe Step 3 decision rule (\"does the answer change which downstream epics exist\n105\tor what they do?\"):\n106\t\n107\t1. **Visibility API RBAC aggregation** (do data scientists hold `view`/`edit`\n108\t   bindings that aggregate `pending-workloads-lq-viewer-role`?): NO — the code\n109\t   handles 403 gracefully either way and both outcomes (position shown vs.\n110\t   silently omitted) are already specified as acceptance criteria on the same\n111\t   epic. The answer only affects later UI-polish investment. Recorded as a\n112\t   validation acceptance criterion on E003.\n113\t2. **Form of the positive Kueue indicator** (banner vs. badge vs. label,\n114\t   RHOAIUX-7470): NO — engineering effort is minimal regardless of choice and\n115\t   development proceeds with placeholder treatment. Recorded as an acceptance\n116\t   criterion on E002, with the design deliverable tracked as E006.\n117\t\n118\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n119\t\n120\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) |\n121\t|-----|----------|---------|\n122\t| Distinguish Preempted from other Eviction reasons in workbench status display | P0 | E001 |\n123\t| Surface Requeued state with retry count and next retry time from `requeueState` | P0 | E001 |\n124\t| Positive Kueue indicator on project details page (`kueue.openshift.io/managed=true`) | P0 | E002, E006 (final treatment) |\n125\t| Anomaly indicator on non-Kueue workloads in Kueue-managed namespaces | P0 | E002, E006 (final treatment) |\n126\t| Display workload scheduling status from Workload CR conditions with human-friendly overrides and raw fallback | P0 | E001, E005 (final copy) |\n127\t| Integrate Kueue Visibility API for queue position display, graceful 403 degradation | P1 | E003 |\n128\t| Fix HardwareProfile details popover for GitOps-managed notebooks | P1 | E004 |\n129\t| `k8sNameRegex` validation on LocalQueue name field in HardwareProfile admin form | P1 | E004 |\n130\t| Info indicator on HP dropdown explaining queue-enabled-only filtering | P1 | E004, E006 (final treatment) |\n131\t| Structured, extensible status derivation model (away from wildcard/substring event matching) | P2 | E001 |\n132\t| Status message granularity: WaitForRecovery vs. WaitForStart, AdmissionCheck pending/retry | P2 | E001 |\n133\t\n134\tAll 11 HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n135\t\n136\t### Priority-split decisions\n137\t\n138\t- The P2 HLRs (structured status model; message granularity) are bundled into\n139\t  E001 rather than split: they share the same status-derivation data\n140\t  structures and implementation surface as the P0 status work, and the\n141\t  Staff-directed architecture (state-driven from Workload CR conditions)\n142\t  makes the structured model the foundation of the P0 display work, not a\n143\t  deferrable add-on. Splitting would force two epics to build the same status\n144\t  model independently.\n145\t- E005 (Content) maps to the P0 status-display HLR and is scored P0: the\n146\t  final human-friendly override wording is the deliverable of that HLR, even\n147\t  though engineering proceeds with placeholder copy (non-blocking).\n148\t- E006 (UXD) maps to the P0 indicator HLRs and is scored P0 by the same\n149\t  logic.\n150\t- E007 (docs-authoring) is exempt from priority inheritance per Step 4;\n151\t  strategy frontmatter `priority: Major` → P1.\n152\t\n153\t## Health Warnings\n154\t\n155\t- **Effort estimate may be optimistic**: the strategy is estimated S (1-3\n156\t  sprints), but commits 11 HLRs across four frontend implementation epics\n157\t  plus three cross-team streams (UXD, Content, Docs). Non-blocking; verify\n158\t  capacity assumptions during epic planning.\n159\t- **AI-generated sections over-promise**: the AI-written Background/Proposed\n160\t  Solution sections describe quota/resource-availability columns, estimated\n161\t  wait times, and historical queue data that Staff input explicitly excludes.\n162\t  Stakeholders reading only the AI sections may expect these; this\n163\t  decomposition follows the Staff input (see overrides above).\n164\t- **Position display may degrade to admin-only**: if RHOAI clusters do not\n165\t  bind data scientists to roles aggregating `pending-workloads-lq-viewer-role`,\n166\t  the P1 queue position feature is effectively admin-only. This is handled by\n167\t  the 403-silent-degradation acceptance criterion on E003, but the\n168\t  cost/benefit of the position UI polish depends on the RBAC validation\n169\t  outcome.\n170\t\n171\t## Tiered Delivery\n172\t\n173\tNot applicable. There is no external dependency with uncertain timing that\n174\tgates user-facing value: the only dependency (UXD designs, RHOAIUX-7470) is\n175\texplicitly non-blocking — implementation proceeds with placeholder copy and\n176\tvisual treatment, replaced when UX delivers.\n177\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bba4ebb031904c7e","agent_id":"acac52a15f485ded0","session_id":"56884f6e-5c85-4514-8d3c-714b4e528234","uuid":"c33364a8-0db7-468f-bbce-d06f3718d157","timestamp":"2026-10-22T09:02:13.390Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9fd3838eed3bca8c","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8002 decomposition"}
