{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d6566efcb518c19","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8002-E001\n3\ttitle: Workload scheduling status model and display in workbenches overview\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8002\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Dashboard\n6\tteam: Dashboard UI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 1\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 1\n15\t  external_dependency: 1\n16\t  human_process_gates: 0\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 7\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Workload Scheduling Status Model and Display in Workbenches Overview\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tRebuild the workbench scheduling status display in the odh-dashboard so it is\n34\tstate-driven from Kueue Workload CR conditions and pod/container statuses,\n35\treplacing the current model that conflates all Evicted conditions as\n36\t\"Preempted\" and relies on wildcard/substring matching of events. This epic\n37\tdelivers the core status derivation logic, the corrected Workload condition\n38\ttyping, the human-friendly message override mechanism (with placeholder\n39\tdefaults), and the rendering of scheduling status in the workbenches overview.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Extend the `WorkloadCondition` type union in `k8sTypes.ts`: add\n44\t  `QuotaReserved`, `Admitted`, `PodsReady`, `Finished`, `Evicted`,\n45\t  `Preempted`, `Requeued`, `BlockedOnPreemptionGates`, `DeactivationTarget`;\n46\t  remove the incorrect `'Failed'` entry (failure is expressed as `Finished`\n47\t  with reason `Failed`).\n48\t- Distinguish Preempted (higher-priority workload took resources) from other\n49\t  Eviction reasons: `PodsReadyTimeout`, `AdmissionCheck`,\n50\t  `ClusterQueueStopped`, `LocalQueueStopped`, `Deactivated`, `NodeFailures`,\n51\t  `MaximumExecutionTimeExceeded`.\n52\t- Surface the Requeued state with retry count and next retry time computed\n53\t  from the Workload's `requeueState` (`requeueAt`, attempt count).\n54\t- Implement a structured, extensible status derivation from Workload CR\n55\t  conditions and pod/container statuses, moving away from hardcoded progress\n56\t  steps and wildcard/substring matching of events.\n57\t- Implement the message override mechanism as a lookup table of\n58\t  human-friendly overrides for known condition/reason combinations, with\n59\t  reasonable engineering-default copy as placeholders until the content\n60\t  review delivers final wording.\n61\t- Improve status message granularity: distinguish WaitForRecovery from\n62\t  WaitForStart; surface AdmissionCheck pending/retry states.\n63\t- Render the derived scheduling status (including eviction reason, requeue\n64\t  retry information, and queue assignment context) in the workbenches\n65\t  overview status column.\n66\t- Preserve workload-to-Notebook matching via\n67\t  `buildWorkloadMapForNotebooks()` in `api/k8s/workloads.ts`\n68\t  (`kueue.x-k8s.io/job-name` label, then `ownerReferences`).\n69\t\n70\t## Acceptance Criteria\n71\t\n72\t- Given a Kueue-managed namespace where a workbench has been evicted due to\n73\t  `ClusterQueueStopped`, when the user views the workbench status, then the\n74\t  status displays \"Evicted\" with reason \"Queue stopped by administrator\" —\n75\t  NOT \"Preempted\", measured by the status label text and variant differing\n76\t  from the Preempted state.\n77\t- Given a workbench has been evicted and the Workload CR has a `Requeued`\n78\t  condition with `requeueState.requeueAt` set, when the user views the\n79\t  workbench status, then the status displays retry information including next\n80\t  retry time and attempt count, measured by the status text including the\n81\t  computed retry time from `requeueState`.\n82\t- Given a workbench's Workload CR has a condition type or reason not\n83\t  recognized by the dashboard's status model, when the workbench status is\n84\t  rendered, then the raw Kueue condition message is displayed rather than a\n85\t  blank state, measured by the status text containing the Workload CR's\n86\t  condition `.message` field content.\n87\t- Unknown condition types are never silently dropped; the `WorkloadCondition`\n88\t  type union extension does not break existing status logic.\n89\t- Backwards compatibility: all changes are purely additive and conditional;\n90\t  existing workbench behavior is unchanged when Kueue is not enabled or the\n91\t  namespace is not Kueue-managed.\n92\t- Human-friendly overrides use engineering-default placeholder copy that is\n93\t  replaceable when the finalized content deliverable lands; the fallback for\n94\t  any uncovered condition/reason combination is always the raw Kueue\n95\t  condition message.\n96\t- Status derivation is state-driven from Workload CR conditions and\n97\t  pod/container statuses; no wildcard/substring matching of events remains in\n98\t  the scheduling status path.\n99\t\n100\t## HLR Traceability\n101\t\n102\t- [P0] Distinguish Preempted from other Eviction reasons\n103\t  (ClusterQueueStopped, LocalQueueStopped, PodsReadyTimeout, Deactivated,\n104\t  etc.) in the workbench status display.\n105\t- [P0] Surface Requeued state with retry count and next retry time from\n106\t  `requeueState` when a workload is evicted and waiting to re-enter the\n107\t  queue.\n108\t- [P0] Display workload scheduling status derived from Workload CR\n109\t  conditions with human-friendly message overrides and raw message fallback\n110\t  (shared with the content deliverable for final wording).\n111\t- [P2] Improve status model progress steps to a structured, extensible\n112\t  status derivation model.\n113\t- [P2] Improve status message granularity: distinguish WaitForRecovery from\n114\t  WaitForStart, surface AdmissionCheck pending/retry states.\n115\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ff23514cd12c266","agent_id":"a338d4df2fc9720fc","session_id":"56884f6e-5c85-4514-8d3c-714b4e528234","uuid":"ce4b6402-17b1-4a0e-8ed8-257589c3f6fe","timestamp":"2026-10-22T09:05:29.976Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d6566efcb518c19","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8002 decomposition"}
