{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-af58ccdb8dde82a5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8002-E002\n3\ttitle: Kueue management indicators for projects and workbenches\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8002\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Dashboard\n6\tteam: Dashboard UI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 1\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 0\n15\t  external_dependency: 1\n16\t  human_process_gates: 0\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Kueue Management Indicators for Projects and Workbenches\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tAdd visibility indicators to the odh-dashboard so users can tell whether\n34\ttheir project uses queue-based scheduling: a positive Kueue indicator on the\n35\tproject details page for Kueue-managed namespaces, and an anomaly indicator\n36\ton individual workbenches that are NOT managed by Kueue inside a Kueue-managed\n37\tnamespace. Development proceeds with a placeholder visual treatment; this\n38\tepic closes with the placeholder in place. Swapping in the final treatment\n39\tonce the UX design deliverable (RHOAIUX-7470) lands is re-scoped to a\n40\tfollow-up task so it cannot block this epic.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\t- Project details page: display a positive indicator (info banner, badge, or\n45\t  label — final form per UX decision, placeholder during development) when\n46\t  the namespace has the `kueue.openshift.io/managed=true` label. The\n47\t  requirement is non-negotiable: users must know their project uses\n48\t  queue-based scheduling because it affects how their workloads start.\n49\t- Workbenches overview: for a namespace that IS Kueue-managed, show a visual\n50\t  anomaly indicator only on workbenches that are NOT managed by Kueue\n51\t  (missing the `kueue.x-k8s.io/queue-name` label — e.g. created via GitOps or\n52\t  CLI bypassing the dashboard). Do NOT show \"managed by Kueue\" on every\n53\t  workload in a Kueue-managed namespace; only the anomaly is flagged.\n54\t- Warning about missing queue labels must never block workload creation.\n55\t\n56\t## Acceptance Criteria\n57\t\n58\t- Given a Kueue-managed namespace, when the user views the project details\n59\t  page, then a positive indicator is visible stating this project uses\n60\t  queue-based scheduling, measured by the indicator element being present in\n61\t  the DOM when the namespace label `kueue.openshift.io/managed=true` exists\n62\t  and absent when it does not.\n63\t- Given a Kueue-managed namespace containing a workbench that does NOT have\n64\t  the `kueue.x-k8s.io/queue-name` label (created via GitOps or CLI without\n65\t  queue assignment), when the user views the workbenches overview, then that\n66\t  specific workbench displays a visual indicator that it is not managed by\n67\t  Kueue, measured by the anomaly indicator being present only on non-Kueue\n68\t  workloads and absent on Kueue-managed workloads.\n69\t- A placeholder visual treatment is in place from the start, rendered through\n70\t  a swappable treatment hook, so this epic closes with the placeholder\n71\t  treatment; integrating the final UX treatment from RHOAIUX-7470 is tracked\n72\t  as a follow-up task once the design delivers and requires no rework of the\n73\t  underlying condition logic.\n74\t- No workload creation is blocked due to a missing queue label; at most a\n75\t  warning is shown.\n76\t\n77\t## HLR Traceability\n78\t\n79\t- [P0] Add positive Kueue indicator on project details page when namespace\n80\t  has `kueue.openshift.io/managed=true` label.\n81\t- [P0] Add anomaly indicator on workloads in a Kueue-managed namespace that\n82\t  are NOT managed by Kueue (missing `kueue.x-k8s.io/queue-name` label).\n83\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ff23514cd12c266","agent_id":"a338d4df2fc9720fc","session_id":"56884f6e-5c85-4514-8d3c-714b4e528234","uuid":"293d4fbc-97ed-4e91-bfcb-d1a0f606cfdb","timestamp":"2026-10-22T09:05:30.800Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-af58ccdb8dde82a5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8002 decomposition"}
