{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-869682aa85c9572a","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8002-E003\n3\ttitle: Kueue Visibility API queue position integration\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8002\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Dashboard\n6\tteam: Dashboard UI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 1\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 0\n15\t  external_dependency: 0\n16\t  human_process_gates: 0\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 4\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Kueue Visibility API Queue Position Integration\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tIntegrate Kueue's Visibility API (`visibility.kueue.x-k8s.io`) into the\n34\todh-dashboard to display queue position for pending workloads in the\n35\tworkbenches overview. Queue position is not a field on the Workload object —\n36\tit lives on the `PendingWorkload` type served by the Visibility API's\n37\t`PendingWorkloadsSummary` subresources on queues. All calls go through the\n38\t`/api/k8s` passthrough proxy with the logged-in user's token and are subject\n39\tto the user's RBAC.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Add a frontend API client for the Kueue Visibility API\n44\t  (`visibility.kueue.x-k8s.io/v1beta2`), reading the `pendingworkloads`\n45\t  subresource on LocalQueues:\n46\t  `GET /apis/visibility.kueue.x-k8s.io/v1beta2/namespaces/{ns}/localqueues/{name}/pendingworkloads`.\n47\t- Display `positionInLocalQueue` (and `positionInClusterQueue` where\n48\t  available) for pending workloads in the workbenches overview.\n49\t- Graceful degradation on 403: a 403 on the Visibility API must fail\n50\t  silently — position info is supplementary, not critical. Use the existing\n51\t  `getGenericErrorCode` pattern from `DistributedWorkloadsContext.tsx`.\n52\t- ClusterQueue-level position (`/clusterqueues/{name}/pendingworkloads`) is\n53\t  cluster-scoped and admin-only; include only if it fits the same mechanism\n54\t  without extra RBAC assumptions.\n55\t- Validate whether RHOAI clusters bind data scientists to Kubernetes roles\n56\t  (`batch-user`, `view`, `admin`, `edit`) that aggregate Kueue's\n57\t  `pending-workloads-lq-viewer-role` ClusterRole, and document the finding\n58\t  for the position-UI polish investment decision.\n59\t- Position fetching is asynchronous and non-blocking: the workbenches\n60\t  overview stays responsive while Visibility API calls are in flight, and\n61\t  position rendering scales to large numbers of queued workloads.\n62\t\n63\t## Acceptance Criteria\n64\t\n65\t- Given a workbench is in QueuingPending state and the user's token has\n66\t  `batch-user` RBAC to the Visibility API, when the workbenches overview page\n67\t  renders, then the queue position is displayed (position in local queue),\n68\t  measured by the position number being present and matching the value from\n69\t  the `pendingworkloads` subresource.\n70\t- Given a workbench is in QueuingPending state and the user's token does NOT\n71\t  have RBAC to the Visibility API, when the workbenches overview page\n72\t  renders, then the queue position is silently omitted with no error\n73\t  displayed, measured by the absence of both position data and error\n74\t  indicators.\n75\t- The RBAC availability validation is documented: if data scientists do not\n76\t  hold aggregating role bindings by default, position display is effectively\n77\t  admin-only and this is recorded as a known limitation (403 handling covers\n78\t  regular users).\n79\t- Given the workbenches overview with Kueue integration active, when\n80\t  Visibility API calls for queue position are in flight, then the UI remains\n81\t  responsive, measured by the overview rendering and remaining interactive\n82\t  without blocking on position fetches (position data loads asynchronously\n83\t  and does not delay the initial render or interactivity of the page).\n84\t- Given a Kueue-managed namespace with a large number of queued workloads\n85\t  (e.g. 100 or more pending workloads across its LocalQueues), when the\n86\t  workbenches overview renders, then queue positions are displayed for all\n87\t  pending workloads without UI degradation, measured by the overview list\n88\t  and position data rendering completely and correctly under that load.\n89\t- Existing workbench behavior is unchanged when Kueue is not enabled.\n90\t\n91\t## HLR Traceability\n92\t\n93\t- [P1] Integrate Kueue Visibility API for queue position display\n94\t  (`positionInLocalQueue`, `positionInClusterQueue`) via\n95\t  `PendingWorkloadsSummary` subresource on LocalQueue — gracefully degrade\n96\t  on 403.\n97\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ff23514cd12c266","agent_id":"a338d4df2fc9720fc","session_id":"56884f6e-5c85-4514-8d3c-714b4e528234","uuid":"a9a2b9a6-cc5a-438d-9c97-f1d4f86b0dfb","timestamp":"2026-10-22T09:05:36.163Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-869682aa85c9572a","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8002 decomposition"}
