w Kueue\n50\t  condition messages are unintelligible to them; the overrides must explain\n51\t  what is happening and what (if anything) the user can do.\n52\t- Deliver the copy in the form consumable by the dashboard's message override\n53\t  lookup table (final wording replaces the engineering placeholders).\n54\t- Incorporate content review feedback from UXD (RHOAIUX-7470).\n55\t\n56\t## Acceptance Criteria\n57\t\n58\t- Every known condition/reason combination in the dashboard's status model\n59\t  has a reviewed human-friendly override; no known combination falls through\n60\t  to the raw message by omission (the raw-message fallback remains for\n61\t  unknown conditions only).\n62\t- Copy is approved through the UXD content review (RHOAIUX-7470).\n63\t- Override wording is delivered in a form that drops into the dashboard's\n64\t  override lookup table without changes to the fallback mechanism.\n65\t\n66\t## HLR Traceability\n67\t\n68\t- [P0] Display workload scheduling status derived from Workload CR\n69\t  conditions with human-friendly message overrides and raw message fallback\n70\t  (final wording; the override mechanism and placeholder copy are delivered\n71\t  by the status model implementation).\n72\t- [P2] Improve status message granularity: distinguish WaitForRecovery from\n73\t  WaitForStart, surface AdmissionCheck pending/retry states (wording for the\n74\t  newly distinguished states).\n75\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ff23514cd12c266","agent_id":"a338d4df2fc9720fc","session_id":"56884f6e-5c85-4514-8d3c-714b4e528234","uuid":"40942e95-b5d7-4e5b-b432-6e8985b0106b","timestamp":"2026-10-22T09:05:40.599Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f59d1eeb4e81816","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8002 decomposition"}
